{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@preconcurrency"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"map","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transformed","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transform","kind":"internalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"@escaping","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci7ElementQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncSequence\/Element"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transformed","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceV","text":"AsyncThrowingMapSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncThrowingMapSequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp","text":"Transformed"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A mapping closure. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transform"},{"text":" accepts an element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"of this sequence as its parameter and returns a transformed value of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"same or of a different type. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transform"},{"type":"text","text":" can also throw an error, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends the transformed sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"transform"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","level":2,"text":"Return Value","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An asynchronous sequence that contains, in order, the elements"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"produced by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transform"},{"text":" closure.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method to transform every element received from a base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous sequence. Typically, you use this to transform from one type"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of element to another.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this example, an asynchronous sequence called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" produces "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"5","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The closure provided to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" and looks up a corresponding "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"romanNumeralDict"},{"type":"text","text":" dictionary. This means the outer "},{"code":"for await in","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" loop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterates over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" instances instead of the underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that "},{"code":"Counter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" produces. Also, the dictionary doesn’t provide a key for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4"},{"type":"text","text":", and the closure throws an error for any key it can’t look up, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receiving this value from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" ends the modified sequence with an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let romanNumeralDict: [Int: String] =","    [1: \"I\", 2: \"II\", 3: \"III\", 5: \"V\"]","","do {","    let stream = Counter(howHigh: 5)","        .map { (value) throws -> String in","            guard let roman = romanNumeralDict[value] else {","                throw MyError()","            }","            return roman","        }","    for try await numeral in stream {","        print(numeral, terminator: \" \")","    }","} catch {","    print(\"Error: \\(error)\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"I II III Error: MyError() \""]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncDropFirstSequence\/map(_:)-7g3xh","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"Swift","relatedModules":[]}],"title":"map(_:)","externalID":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF::SYNTHESIZED::s:12_Concurrency22AsyncDropFirstSequenceV","extendedModule":"_Concurrency","platforms":[{"beta":false,